Nonsense. You're declaring it to use the font "Symbol"; this is _not_
the same thing as saying "these characters are Greek", you're relying
on the reader to have the exact particular font you have in mind.

Try changing it to '&Kappa;&rho;&omicron;&iota;&sigma;&omicron;&sigmaf;'.
These are the appropriate HTML entities.

(For short pieces of Greek text where you're not worried about
accents; if you wanted to do Greek at length, you'd want to use
ISO8859-7 or Unicode, properly declared as such.)

> On your computer, lacking the correct font, these characters are shown as
> KroisoV.

